  {
   "tipo": "explicacion",
   "titulo": "Age with «zijn» and months",
   "texto": [
    "Unlike Spanish (using «have»), in Dutch age is expressed with the verb «zijn» (being / being): «Ik ben twintig jaar» (I am twenty years old). To ask: «Hoe oud ben je?» (How old are you?). The «jarig»: «Wanneer ben je jarig?» adjective is used for the birthday, and is responded to by the «in»: «In mei» preposition (In May)."
   ]
  },
